# Backend enums

When adding or changing C# in `api/` or `worker/`, use an enum for a closed
set that Cardui defines and branches on. Do this in the same change as the
value.

- Give each enum its own file. Name the file after the enum.
- A value stored on an entity lives in `Models`. A value used by domain
  rules lives in `Domain`. Do not put an enum under `Services`.
- Do not nest an enum in a class, record, service, controller, or calculator.
- An enum used by only one caller may be `internal`.
- The member name is the stored text and the JSON text. Do not store or
  return the numeric value.
- Persist with `HasConversion<string>()`. Serialize with
  `CarduiJsonSerializer.UseEnumMemberNames`, which writes the member name
  and rejects a number.
- A value an outside system can extend, a user-defined key, or a slug whose
  text is not the member name stays a string constant. Account type,
  account subtype, category keys, and account group keys stay strings.
- A display name stays a string constant. It is not an enum member.

```csharp
public enum FinancialRecordSource
{
    Plaid,
    Manual,
    Csv
}
```
